     "text": "{\"cost\": 5, \"rationale\": \"Entry footholds are free and are not counted. One shortest path takes 5 steps: h1_1:escalate (AND of edge0 and edge1), h1_0:access (OR from an entry), h2_2:reach (AND of h1_1, h1_0 and edge1), h4_0:traverse (OR from h2_2), then crown:obtain. Two other 5-step paths exist: through h4_2:pivot from h2_2, or h1_1, h2_1, h3_1, h4_1, crown. No 4-step path exists. Crown needs one h4 step. h4_0 and h4_2 need h2_2 or h2_0 (h3_0 itself needs h2_0), and both of those need h1_1 and h1_0. h4_1 needs h3_1, which needs h1_1 and h2_1.\"}"
